                                "sense_id": "b4473b29-5c51-3271-9769-3162cb79fe34",
                                "text": "1922, Rudyard Kipling, \"A St. Helena Lullaby,\" lines 17-20, in Rudyard Kipling's Verse, Garden City: Doubleday, http://www.bartleby.com/364/294.html\n\"How far is St. Helena from the Capes of Trafalgar?\" / A longish way—a longish way—with ten year more to run. / It's South across the water underneath a falling star. / (What you cannot finish you must leave undone!)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6647958c-4610-4163-afec-4d52f29a265a",
                                "sense_id": "b4473b29-5c51-3271-9769-3162cb79fe34",
                                "text": "She had a longish face scribbled all over with wrinkles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56a5d34a-4941-4c33-bfec-b183af93b918",
                                "sense_id": "b4473b29-5c51-3271-9769-3162cb79fe34",
                                "text": "It was a longish time before I received a reply to my letter."
